\"col-md-7\" style=\"width: 770px; padding-right: 7.5px; padding-left: 7.5px; margin-top: 0px; position: relative; min-height: 1px; float: left;\"><div class=\"welcome-text px-3\"><h2 class=\"section-title mb-3 text-primary font-weight-bold\" style=\"margin: 0px 0px 1rem; font-weight: bold; color: rgb(25, 135, 84); text-transform: uppercase; padding: 0px;\">About AYUSH</h2><div class=\"mb-4\" style=\"text-align: justify; width: 60px; height: 4px; background-color: rgb(0, 123, 94); margin-bottom: 1rem !important;\"></div><p class=\"text-justify text-muted\" style=\"margin: 0px 0px 1rem; line-height: 1.87; font-size: 16px; text-align: justify; line-break: anywhere; color: rgb(108, 117, 125) !important;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">Ayurveda, Yoga &amp; Naturopathy, Unani, Siddha, and Homoeopathy</span> streams of medicine come under AYUSH. Health care delivery through these systems is facilitated by various institutions under the Department of AYUSH. The department provides medical aid through a network of <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">735 dispensaries, 4 Mini-Hospitals, and 4 AYUSH Teaching Hospitals</span> across Andhra Pradesh.</p><p class=\"text-justify text-muted\" style=\"margin: 0px 0px 1rem; line-height: 1.87; font-size: 16px; text-align: justify; line-break: anywhere; color: rgb(108, 117, 125) !important;\">With immense pride and commitment, AYUSH serves nearly 5 crore people throughout the state, focusing on preventive, promotive, and curative aspects of healthcare.</p></div></div></div></div></section>\";s:4:\"file\";N;s:9:\"file_icon\";N;s:6:\"status\";i:1;s:10:\"created_by\";N;s:10:\"updated_by\";i:1;s:10:\"deleted_by\";N;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-24 11:06:30\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-24 12:04:30\";s:10:\"deleted_at\";N;s:8:\"children\";O:29:\"Illuminate\\Support\\Collection\":2:{s:8:\"\0*\0items\";a:0:{}s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;}}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:39:{s:2:\"id\";i:28;s:7:\"menu_id\";i:1;s:9:\"